---

<DocsLayout
  title="Architecture"
  subtitle="Pure geometry in packages/core. I/O in the sidecar. The window is a client of the HTTP contract."
  description="CADCAMFUN repository architecture, dependency direction, work-package status, and process boundaries."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="direction" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Direction</h2>
    <p>{dependencyNote}</p>
    <p>
      Spec <code>00-overview.md</code> §3 is the layout contract. Libraries live under
      <code>packages/</code>. Processes live under <code>apps/</code>. Specs in
      <code>specs/</code> win on contracts. When a task cites the roadmap, sequence comes from
      <code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code> (RM-00–RM-11). The current step recorded there is RM-01,
      the action catalogue.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Package</th><th>Path</th><th>May do</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/core</code></td><td><code>packages/core</code></td><td>CAD, technical drawing, and CAM algorithms over readonly data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/api</code></td><td><code>packages/api</code></td><td>HttpApi groups, shared schemas, generated client</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/db</code></td><td><code>packages/db</code></td><td>Drizzle schema, migrations, <code>Database</code> service</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/ai</code></td><td><code>packages/ai</code></td><td>nikcli host and AI SDK v7, as Effect services</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/plugin-sdk</code></td><td><code>packages/plugin-sdk</code></td><td>Manifest, capabilities, <code>definePlugin</code>, test host</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/vcs</code></td><td><code>packages/vcs</code></td><td>Git objects, repository, JSON merge, GitHub transport</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/workflow</code></td><td><code>packages/workflow</code></td><td>Workflow schema, triggers, runner</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/sidecar</code></td><td><code>apps/sidecar</code></td><td>Handlers, repositories, layers, plugin host</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/desktop</code></td><td><code>apps/desktop</code></td><td>SolidJS UI and the Rust shell</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@cadcamfun/mobile</code></td><td><code>apps/mobile</code></td><td>Expo client of a paired desktop</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <code>packages/core/src/index.ts</code> exports CAD flat and as <code>cad</code>, CAM only as
      <code>cam</code>, and technical drawings as <code>drawing</code>. CAD and CAM both define
      names such as <code>Move</code> and <code>Path</code>, so a flat CAM export would collide.
      Drawing helpers live under <code>packages/core/src/drawing</code>
      (<code>project.ts</code>, <code>section.ts</code>, <code>dimensions.ts</code>,
      <code>sheet.ts</code>, <code>svg.ts</code>).
    </p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Imports a caller actually uses">
{`import { cad, cam, drawing } from "@cadcamfun/core"
import { Database, schema } from "@cadcamfun/db"
import { ApiClient } from "@cadcamfun/api"`}
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="work-packages" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Work packages</h2>
    <p>
      Status text below is the task board in <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §4. A row marked
      done still has the limits written in its own spec. HTTP and UI parity with the legacy app
      are requirements, and they are unfinished.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>WP</th><th>Owns</th><th>Board status</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>WP0</td><td><code>packages/db</code></td><td>in progress — adding <code>LocalKeyValue</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP1</td><td><code>packages/core/src/cad</code></td><td>done (288 core tests incl. WP2)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP2</td><td><code>packages/core/src/cam</code></td><td>done (posts, goldens, legacy-bug regressions)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP3</td><td><code>packages/api</code></td><td>in progress — 67/195 legacy route files in the contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP4</td><td><code>apps/sidecar</code></td><td>in progress — every contract group is served; families without a contract are still missing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP5</td><td><code>apps/desktop/src-tauri</code></td><td>M1 done (clippy + 32 Rust tests; verified with a stub sidecar)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP6</td><td><code>apps/desktop/src/app</code>, screens</td><td>in progress — core screens exist; the rest of the legacy pages are still stubs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP7</td><td><code>apps/desktop/src/viewport</code></td><td>in progress</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP8</td><td><code>packages/ai</code></td><td>done</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP9</td><td><code>packages/plugin-sdk</code>, <code>apps/sidecar/src/plugins</code></td><td>done for SDK + host; SDK host is not exposed over HTTP yet</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP10</td><td>workflows, <code>scripts/</code>, updater</td><td>done for pipeline + CI + updater; release secrets unset</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP11</td><td><code>packages/vcs</code></td><td>done for core + sidecar + API; desktop panels and GitHub routes pending</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP12</td><td><code>packages/workflow</code></td><td>done for engine + runner; the board says only <code>project/*</code> steps are registered</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP13</td><td><code>apps/mobile</code></td><td>Expo migration integrated; native Release/device validation in progress; TestFlight pending</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WP14</td><td>multi-operation setups</td><td>in progress — planner contracts claimed on the board; desktop store and persistence pending</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Parity is a requirement, and it is open">
      <p>
        Spec 00 §6 requires the same HTTP API as the legacy app (195 route files in
        <code>specs/api-inventory.md</code>) and a SolidJS UI that matches the legacy screens.
        Spec 05 records that about 15% of those route files are served. Do not treat a green
        package test as finished product parity.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="processes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Processes</h2>
    <p>
      Tauri’s Rust process does not run <code>bun:sqlite</code>. Spec 00 §2 keeps Effect and Drizzle
      in a Bun-compiled sidecar (<code>bun build --compile</code>). Rust owns the window, tray,
      menus, updater, secure storage, and sidecar lifecycle. Spec <code>07-tauri-shell.md</code>
      records the ready line the sidecar prints after migrations:
    </p>
    <DocCode language="text" title="Sidecar stdout after listen">
{`{"event":"ready","port":N}`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      The shell generates a per-launch token, passes <code>CADCAMFUN_TOKEN</code> and
      <code>CADCAMFUN_DATA_DIR</code>, and the webview calls the sidecar over HTTP on
      <code>127.0.0.1</code>. Spec 05 requires every request to carry
      <code>Authorization: Bearer</code>. Failure to start prints
      <code>&#123;"event":"error","message":"…"&#125;</code> and exits non-zero. The sidecar exits
      when stdin closes and on <code>SIGTERM</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="note" title="WP5 on the task board">
      <p>
        WP5 is M1 done (clippy + 32 Rust tests; verified with a stub sidecar). Spec 07 §7 records
        later menu, tray, secrets, and lifecycle work on top of that milestone, and a focused
        check of 60 Rust tests with 2 ignored. Do not read M1 as a finished signed release.
        Packaged updater verification and signing stay with WP10.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="desktop-source" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Desktop source</h2>
    <p>
      <code>apps/desktop/src/app</code> is the shell, the route table, and the API client
      (<code>App.tsx</code>, <code>Shell.tsx</code>, <code>routes.tsx</code>, <code>client.ts</code>,
      <code>sidecar.ts</code>). <code>src/pages</code> are one-line adapters. A page re-exports a
      screen and holds no product logic.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each product area is <code>src/features/&lt;name&gt;</code>. Directories present:
      <code>admin</code>, <code>ai</code>, <code>analytics</code>, <code>auth</code>,
      <code>billing</code>, <code>cad</code>, <code>cam</code>, <code>chat</code>,
      <code>companion</code>, <code>costs</code>, <code>dashboard</code>, <code>legal</code>,
      <code>library</code>, <code>marketplace</code>, <code>mcp</code>, <code>organizations</code>,
      <code>plugins</code>, <code>profile</code>, <code>projects</code>, <code>settings</code>,
      <code>toolpaths</code>. Shared UI is <code>src/shared</code> (<code>ui</code>,
      <code>components</code>, <code>state</code>). The 2D and 3D engines are
      <code>src/viewport</code>. Strings go through <code>src/i18n</code>. The fake API used while
      a group has no live handler is <code>src/testing</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Spec 06 says the working end-to-end screens are Projects, CAD, CAM, Library, and Settings.
      Routes such as <code>/materials</code>, <code>/tools</code>, <code>/machine</code>,
      <code>/toolpaths</code>, <code>/costs</code>, <code>/ai</code>, and <code>/plugins</code>
      exist in <code>routes.tsx</code>. The long tail of legacy pages are still stubs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>packages/core</code> must not open SQLite, the network, or the filesystem, and must not import <code>.reference/</code>.</li>
      <li><code>packages/api</code> must not contain server handlers or a database client.</li>
      <li><code>apps/desktop</code> must not query Drizzle. It talks to the sidecar through the API contract.</li>
      <li><code>apps/desktop/src-tauri</code> must not contain toolpath or solid math.</li>
      <li>Only <code>apps/sidecar/src/config.ts</code> reads process configuration. Other modules receive it through the <code>cadcamfun/AppConfig</code> service.</li>
      <li>Only <code>packages/db</code> talks to SQLite. Hot geometry stays plain functions.</li>
      <li>An agent edits the directory its work package owns. Cross-package contract changes go through the spec first.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <DocRelated items={[{ title: "Stack", href: "/docs/stack" }, { title: "Sidecar", href: "/docs/sidecar" }, { title: "Packages and apps", href: "/docs/packages" }]} />
</DocsLayout>
